Subject: [PATCH] wifi: uwe5622: publish the permanent PHY address

Interface creation selects a valid MAC but never publishes the base
address through wiphy. Consequently the PHY macaddress sysfs attribute
remains zero, and OpenWrt derives an invalid default BSSID from it.

Set perm_addr before registering the wiphy. Use the same source priority
as interface creation: a valid Sunxi platform address, when enabled,
followed by the address returned in the firmware information response.
Do not derive the permanent address from a mutable interface address.

--- a/unisocwifi/main.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/main.c
@@ -1578,6 +1578,12 @@ int sprdwl_core_init(struct device *dev,
 	sprdwl_setup_wiphy(wiphy, priv);
 	sprdwl_vendor_init(wiphy);
 	set_wiphy_dev(wiphy, dev);
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SUNXI_ADDR_MGT)
+	get_custom_mac_address(1, "wifi", wiphy->perm_addr);
+#endif
+	if (!is_valid_ether_addr(wiphy->perm_addr) &&
+	    is_valid_ether_addr(priv->mac_addr))
+		ether_addr_copy(wiphy->perm_addr, priv->mac_addr);
 	ret = wiphy_register(wiphy);
 	if (ret) {
 		wl_err("failed to regitster wiphy(%d)!\n", ret);
